Maya Chen: Heads up, expo sample app is crashing on iOS when using the new JS SDK (ESM build). App freezes after the first generation request. Metro logs `getrandom` errors and then a network 401 with an auth refresh loop.

Liam O'Connor: Which SDK version and expo/devclient? Can you paste the exact Metro error?

Maya Chen: @Liam Using @redwood/inference@0.9.2-alpha, Expo SDK 48, Hermes enabled. Repro steps: run `expo start --dev-client`, open iOS dev client, tap "Generate" in the sample. Console: 
```
> Unable to resolve module 'node:crypto'
> Error: getRandomValues not available
Unhandled promise rejection: TypeError: can't set headers of undefined
fetch /v1/generate -> 401
AuthRetry: refresh token loop (token refresh succeeded but retried request 401s)
```

Sanjay Patel: Two likely things: (1) missing `getrandom` / crypto polyfill for RN/Hermes, (2) the SDK retry logic isn't preserving the request body for RN fetch retries -> backend sees empty body and returns 401/400 depending on auth middleware. We ran into the same with streaming bodies before.

Tasha Rivera: For the crypto bit, add `react-native-get-random-values` (or `expo-random`) and the `global.crypto = require('crypto').webcrypto` shim depending on Metro. Also ensure `rn-getrandom` is in `extraNodeModules` so Metro resolves it.

Oliver Wu: FYI ESM/CJS friction here too. When people switch to ESM import like `import { createClient } from '@redwood/inference'` in RN builds it sometimes resolves to the ESM entry with node:crypto imports. Quick workaround is to import the CJS build path in RN until we ship an RN-safe ESM bundle: `import { createClient } from '@redwood/inference/dist/cjs/index.js'` (not pretty but works).

Maya Chen: Adding logs + stacktrace here: 
```
TypeError: undefined is not an object (evaluating 'req.headers.set')
 at retryRequest (node_modules/@redwood/inference/dist/index.js:842:21)
 at sendRequest (node_modules/@redwood/inference/dist/index.js:776:12)
 at generate (src/api/generate.ts:34:5)
```

Sanjay Patel: That exact `req.headers.set` means the retry wrapper replaced the fetch init with a stream the RN fetch impl can't clone. In browsers we clone bodies, but RN's fetch (and polyfills) don't support cloning ReadableStreams. The fix we discussed in the SDK PR was to buffer the body in memory for RN (ArrayBuffer) before retrying. I opened a draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/487 (WIP) — it buffers `init.body` when `isReactNative()` is true.

Tasha Rivera: Metro config snippet that helped me for expo devclient: 
```js
// metro.config.js
const { getDefaultConfig } = require('expo/metro-config');
const defaultConfig = getDefaultConfig(__dirname);

defaultConfig.resolver.extraNodeModules = {
  ...defaultConfig.resolver.extraNodeModules,
  'react-native-get-random-values': require.resolve('react-native-get-random-values'),
};n
module.exports = defaultConfig;
```

Also add at top of App.tsx: `import 'react-native-get-random-values'` and `import '@react-native/polyfill-global'` for older Hermes.

Oliver Wu: For TypeScript issues (people seeing `Cannot find name 'Blob'` or DOM types), don't add `lib.dom` globally since that can break other RN types. Instead add a small `types/globals.d.ts` in the sample: 
```ts
// types/globals.d.ts
declare global {
  interface Blob {}
  interface ReadableStream {}
}
export {};
```
And include `typeRoots`/`include` for the sample tsconfig.

Maya Chen: Thanks, the crypto polyfill + global types fixed part of it, but the 401 retry still happening. Tried the manual buffer patch locally: it fixed the retry. Can we publish a hotfix?

Sanjay Patel: I'll spin up the PR from draft -> hotfix branch. Short-term patch I used as a wrapper if you need it immediately (place in your app, wraps global.fetch): 
```js
// rn-fetch-retry-patch.js
const originalFetch = global.fetch;
global.fetch = async (input, init = {}) => {
  // if body is a stream, read to buffer for RN fetch retries
  if (init && init.body && typeof init.body.getReader === 'function') {
    const reader = init.body.getReader();
    const chunks = [];
    let done, value;
    while (!(done = (await reader.read()).done)) {
      value = value || (await reader.read()).value; // crude loop for example
      chunks.push(value);
    }
    const buffer = Buffer.concat(chunks);
    init.body = buffer;
  }
  return originalFetch(input, init);
};
```
Note: crude, but works as temporary workaround. We'll refine in the SDK.

ci-bot: CI: expo-samples/ios build failed on main with `@redwood/inference@0.9.2-alpha` — failing tests: sample-app-e2e (see CI logs).

Liam O'Connor: Action items: (1) Sanjay convert PR to hotfix and publish 0.9.3-hotfix, (2) DevEx update expo sample README with metro + crypto instructions + the TS global stub, (3) Oliver open follow-up to publish an RN-safe ESM build or adjust package.json exports to have a `react-native` field.

Tasha Rivera: I'll update the sample app docs and add the `rn-fetch-retry-patch` snippet under troubleshooting.

Maya Chen: Great — will test the hotfix branch once published and report back. Thanks everyone :pray:

Oliver Wu: Also logging note: add a clearer error when retry fails due to uncloneable body so users don't hit silent 401 loops. Filed https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/issues/512.

Maya Chen: tagging @SRE in case any infra flags on repeated 401s show up in monitoring.

(End of thread)
